    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d135">

                <pb facs="0390" n="258" xml:id="pg258"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">819.415C/75: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-06-25T11:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 25,
                                1926—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 2:30
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>43. The Foreign Office telegraphed to the Chargé d’Affaires of Honduras at Panama
                    June 22, prior to the receipt of your telegram No. 21, June 22, 6 p.m.,
                    requesting a report regarding Trejo’s reported actions.</p>
                <p>The Minister for Foreign Affairs has expressed regrets. He states that Trejo was
                    not acting under instructions, that disavowal will be published this afternoon
                    and that Trejo has ceased to be the [delegate of Honduras].</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
